1
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,200
[The content, events, techniques, and outcomes of massage depicted in this series]

2
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:09,411
[are entirely fictional and intended for entertainment purposes only.]

3
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:11,000
[They should not be used as medical advice or as a reference for traditional Thai massage.]

4
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,141
[Viewer discretion is advised. Do not attempt to imitate any of the techniques shown,]

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,151
[as doing so may result in injury.]

6
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:14,161
[Massage services should only be provided by practitioners]

7
00:00:14,170 --> 00:00:15,171
[who are legally licensed and registered.]

8
00:00:16,942 --> 00:00:20,560
Ittha, Pingkhala, Sumana,

9
00:00:20,864 --> 00:00:22,160
Kalathari,

10
00:00:22,427 --> 00:00:24,240
Sahatsarangsi,

11
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:25,881
Thawari,

12
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,760
Chanthaphusang,

13
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,301
Rucham,

14
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:30,920
Sukhumang, and

15
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,600
Sikhini.

16
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:37,360
Massage—an ancient practice passed down through generations.

17
00:00:37,502 --> 00:00:39,760
The art of healing

18
00:00:39,896 --> 00:00:41,440
through precise touch.

19
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,560
Whether squeezing,

20
00:00:44,014 --> 00:00:45,015
pressing,

21
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:46,361
pulling,

22
00:00:46,454 --> 00:00:47,455
stretching,

23
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:48,961
or kneading.

24
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,640
But when two best friends

25
00:00:52,744 --> 00:00:54,640
succumb to the darkness within

26
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:58,600
and discover a forbidden art never known before,

27
00:00:59,096 --> 00:01:00,920
the power to heal is transformed

28
00:01:01,011 --> 00:01:03,012
into a weapon of revenge.

29
00:01:04,046 --> 00:01:07,160
The line between saving a life and taking one

30
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:09,520
can be crossed with a mere turn of the hand.

31
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:14,200
Therapeutic touch

32
00:01:14,374 --> 00:01:17,760
becomes a way to kill with bare hands, leaving no trace,

33
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,990
before the victim even realizes what is happening.

34
00:01:23,582 --> 00:01:25,600
When the dark art of deadly massage...

35
00:01:26,067 --> 00:01:29,920
an undiscovered forbidden practice is used as a weapon,

36
00:01:30,512 --> 00:01:33,800
it turns a healer into a murderer.

37
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:37,720
The only way to stop it is to...

38
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:39,321
destroy it.

39
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,600
[DO NOT READ]

40
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:52,920
[PHUKET, 2011]

41
00:02:59,472 --> 00:03:00,473
Ease in.

42
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:02,601
Apply pressure.

43
00:03:03,947 --> 00:03:04,948
Hold.

44
00:03:09,848 --> 00:03:10,984
The Ten Principal Sen Lines—

45
00:03:11,592 --> 00:03:13,640
the body’s primary energy pathways.

46
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,320
Ittha runs along the left.

47
00:03:17,696 --> 00:03:20,600
Pingkhala runs along the right.

48
00:03:21,632 --> 00:03:24,640
The areas that must never be massaged are extremely important.

49
00:03:25,248 --> 00:03:26,880
Commit them to memory.

50
00:03:27,650 --> 00:03:28,651
The temples.

51
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:30,121
The neck.

52
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:31,961
The armpits.

53
00:03:33,947 --> 00:03:37,640
Coordinate your breathing with the pressure you apply

54
00:03:38,136 --> 00:03:40,400
to control how long each press is held.

55
00:03:40,899 --> 00:03:43,800
Pressure duration is divided into short and long cycles.

56
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:47,960
A short cycle lasts 10 to 15 seconds.

57
00:03:49,566 --> 00:03:50,720
12…

58
00:03:51,288 --> 00:03:52,560
13…

59
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,201
14…

60
00:03:54,835 --> 00:03:56,000
15…

61
00:04:00,334 --> 00:04:01,840
Awesome!

62
00:04:04,499 --> 00:04:05,500
Wow!

63
00:04:18,019 --> 00:04:19,020
All done, sir.

64
00:04:30,275 --> 00:04:31,276
Thank you.

65
00:04:32,654 --> 00:04:33,655
Thank you, sir.

66
00:04:35,518 --> 00:04:36,960
Would you like to work for me?

67
00:04:39,382 --> 00:04:40,383
What do you say?

68
00:04:41,296 --> 00:04:43,440
You’d supervise hundreds of massage therapists.

69
00:04:44,358 --> 00:04:45,359
Interested?

70
00:04:48,603 --> 00:04:51,280
Thank you, but as it happens,

71
00:04:53,158 --> 00:04:54,680
I’ve just opened a place of my own.

72
00:04:56,182 --> 00:04:57,183
Here’s my business card.

73
00:05:02,672 --> 00:05:04,560
The beach there is very peaceful.

74
00:05:05,259 --> 00:05:07,260
Please come and visit sometime.

75
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,760
I’ll take my leave now. Goodbye.

76
00:05:10,123 --> 00:05:11,124
Goodbye.

77
00:05:16,624 --> 00:05:17,920
He dared to turn you down.

78
00:05:21,328 --> 00:05:22,600
Should we kill the bastard?

79
00:05:24,918 --> 00:05:25,919
Hey!

80
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,621
I’m not opening a massage parlor.

81
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:40,720
Please go here, my dad is the best.

82
00:05:40,899 --> 00:05:42,360
Oh, your shop?

83
00:05:42,723 --> 00:05:44,000
Our family's shop.

84
00:05:44,248 --> 00:05:45,249
Wow.

85
00:05:46,686 --> 00:05:47,880
Thank you so much.

86
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,280
Thank you.

87
00:05:49,427 --> 00:05:50,428
Thank you.

88
00:05:51,416 --> 00:05:53,320
- Bye.
- Bye.

89
00:06:10,968 --> 00:06:13,400
Hey, did you see my money? It blew over this way.

90
00:06:17,144 --> 00:06:18,800
Have you seen it?

91
00:06:20,336 --> 00:06:22,840
- Did you see my money?
- No.

92
00:06:25,728 --> 00:06:28,704
Are you crying? What’s wrong? Are you sick?

93
00:06:28,811 --> 00:06:30,846
I have a headache. Leave me alone.

94
00:06:41,891 --> 00:06:42,892
What are you doing?

95
00:06:42,915 --> 00:06:45,200
Stay still. Massaging this spot will make it go away.

96
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:22,160
Does that feel better?

97
00:07:26,254 --> 00:07:28,080
This is my dad’s shop. You can stop by sometime.

98
00:07:43,862 --> 00:07:45,691
Patrick. Patrick, come on.

99
00:07:45,760 --> 00:07:47,200
Let's go to see your father.

100
00:07:47,261 --> 00:07:49,100
I have something to talk to him. Hurry up.

101
00:08:17,326 --> 00:08:18,327
All done.

102
00:08:23,230 --> 00:08:24,440
So you’ve opened your new shop.

103
00:08:24,491 --> 00:08:26,920
Does that mean you won’t come to my house to massage me anymore?

104
00:08:28,304 --> 00:08:29,720
I still can.

105
00:08:31,403 --> 00:08:33,680
But I’d rather you come to my shop.

106
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,280
The atmosphere there is wonderful.

107
00:08:36,816 --> 00:08:38,600
You’ll feel much more relaxed.

108
00:08:38,843 --> 00:08:39,844
All right.

109
00:08:40,219 --> 00:08:41,240
Congratulations.

110
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:42,881
Thank you.

111
00:08:56,891 --> 00:08:58,360
Let’s go, sis!

112
00:08:58,656 --> 00:09:01,168
Did you get into the wrong one? I’m your mother.

113
00:09:04,288 --> 00:09:05,889
- Should we go?
- Let's go.

114
00:09:11,763 --> 00:09:13,200
Mom! That's Dad!

115
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,301
- Dad!
- Korn.

116
00:09:25,251 --> 00:09:26,360
I’m off, then.

117
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,560
- Does it smell good?
- It does.

118
00:09:57,819 --> 00:09:59,040
Phak’s here.

119
00:10:01,128 --> 00:10:02,920
- Why don't you go and see him, sweetheart?
- Phak!

120
00:10:04,974 --> 00:10:05,975
Where have you been?

121
00:10:08,286 --> 00:10:09,287
Oh, my brilliant engineer!

122
00:10:10,710 --> 00:10:13,240
Phak!

123
00:10:13,344 --> 00:10:15,915
I thought you said things were hectic at the construction site. How did you get here?

124
00:10:15,979 --> 00:10:17,020
I slipped away for a bit, Mom.

125
00:10:17,099 --> 00:10:19,600
They’re definitely going to dock your pay.

126
00:10:20,979 --> 00:10:22,720
Minkheng, come help me.

127
00:10:22,856 --> 00:10:23,857
Sure.

128
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:27,720
Here. Pick whichever color you like.

129
00:10:27,770 --> 00:10:28,880
Everyone, take one bowl.

130
00:10:29,566 --> 00:10:30,567
What are you doing, son?

131
00:10:30,606 --> 00:10:33,200
- Just take one and follow me.
- What? All right, take one.

132
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:34,261
Just play along with him.

133
00:10:34,456 --> 00:10:35,457
Follow me.

134
00:10:39,331 --> 00:10:41,960
Dad, you go first.

135
00:10:42,590 --> 00:10:44,899
Me? What am I supposed to do?

136
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:48,960
Put your palm print on this sign to mark it as yours.

137
00:11:11,078 --> 00:11:12,360
That looks beautiful.

138
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,040
Hattha has the tiniest handprint of all.

139
00:11:24,107 --> 00:11:26,040
May we all be blessed with good health,

140
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:28,120
may our business prosper.

141
00:11:28,342 --> 00:11:29,480
And may everyone be happy.

142
00:11:31,043 --> 00:11:32,044
Sathu.

143
00:11:46,371 --> 00:11:48,000
Mom and I embroidered it together.

144
00:11:50,880 --> 00:11:53,350
- We kept it a secret.
- You never told me about this.

145
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,616
How could it be a surprise if we told you?

146
00:11:56,563 --> 00:11:59,000
It belongs to all of us, just like you always say.

147
00:12:00,339 --> 00:12:02,734
- Thank you.
- You two finally did it.

148
00:12:03,432 --> 00:12:04,560
Thank you both so much.

149
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:06,761
And thank you too.

150
00:12:07,761 --> 00:12:08,762
Thank you too.

151
00:12:18,414 --> 00:12:19,415
What?

152
00:12:19,955 --> 00:12:20,956
When?

153
00:12:21,208 --> 00:12:22,209
I’m coming right now.

154
00:12:22,856 --> 00:12:24,960
Dad, I need to go to the construction site.

155
00:12:26,467 --> 00:12:27,468
Is something wrong, son?

156
00:12:28,302 --> 00:12:29,600
The building at the construction site collapsed.

157
00:12:29,704 --> 00:12:30,920
Was anyone hurt?

158
00:12:31,086 --> 00:12:32,640
I don’t know yet. I have to go.

159
00:12:43,363 --> 00:12:45,920
At present, unauthorized personnel are strictly prohibited

160
00:12:45,964 --> 00:12:47,520
from entering the area.

161
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:49,260
If another incident occurs,

162
00:12:49,290 --> 00:12:50,680
the situation could become even more complicated.

163
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:52,960
We have instructed

164
00:12:53,083 --> 00:12:55,880
the forensic team to collect as much evidence as possible.

165
00:12:56,502 --> 00:12:58,560
The cause of the collapse remains unknown.

166
00:12:58,667 --> 00:13:01,300
Meanwhile, the engineer responsible for the design and construction supervision

167
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:03,040
has not yet provided any information.

168
00:13:03,142 --> 00:13:06,566
We will report further details as soon as they become available.

169
00:13:09,936 --> 00:13:11,300
Is that Phak?

170
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:15,981
Go!

171
00:13:17,291 --> 00:13:19,560
What the hell are you going to do? I told you to admit you were at fault.

172
00:13:19,729 --> 00:13:22,000
I already told you, I did nothing wrong. I’m not going, no matter what.

173
00:13:25,686 --> 00:13:26,687
Give it to me.

174
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:33,880
Pha, I need to go see our son.

175
00:13:37,902 --> 00:13:39,003
I'm coming with you.

176
00:13:39,459 --> 00:13:40,460
Don't go!

177
00:13:48,771 --> 00:13:49,772
Hattha!

178
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,121
Dad!

179
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:08,960
Hey, come here!

180
00:14:18,544 --> 00:14:20,200
Hattha, go back inside.

181
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:22,400
No! I need to see Phak.

182
00:14:25,566 --> 00:14:26,567
Fine, let's go.

183
00:14:33,379 --> 00:14:34,720
It's your customer's house.

184
00:14:46,939 --> 00:14:47,940
Hey!

185
00:14:51,467 --> 00:14:52,468
Come here.

186
00:14:53,568 --> 00:14:54,569
Hattha.

187
00:14:55,334 --> 00:14:57,648
- Wait here, I will be right back.
- Dad.

188
00:14:57,660 --> 00:15:00,200
Listen to me, okay? Wait for me here.

189
00:15:28,739 --> 00:15:30,520
Sign the admission of liability and get this over with.

190
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:32,481
I won’t sign it.

191
00:15:33,184 --> 00:15:34,680
You’re the ones who should be held responsible.

192
00:15:34,806 --> 00:15:36,170
I warned you about the steel.

193
00:15:36,459 --> 00:15:39,320
You knew about it, but you did nothing.

194
00:15:39,595 --> 00:15:41,850
I told you to fix the problem.

195
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:43,520
And you promised you would.

196
00:15:43,808 --> 00:15:47,400
You were more afraid the project would be shut down and you’d lose your job.

197
00:15:47,744 --> 00:15:49,045
You piece of shit. Sign it!

198
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:51,464
- Sign it!
- No!

199
00:16:01,022 --> 00:16:02,520
What are you doing?

200
00:16:03,318 --> 00:16:04,240
Okay, okay.

201
00:16:04,470 --> 00:16:05,720
Turn around and get up slowly.

202
00:16:06,326 --> 00:16:07,327
Hurry up!

203
00:16:08,203 --> 00:16:09,204
Give me the phone.

204
00:16:09,638 --> 00:16:11,360
- I just took pictures of the house. It's pretty.
- Hurry!

205
00:16:12,235 --> 00:16:15,280
[WARNING: The massage techniques depicted in this series are fictional.
Do not attempt to imitate them.]

206
00:16:22,422 --> 00:16:24,480
Hattha, press the line on his neck.

207
00:16:24,550 --> 00:16:25,920
That’s a forbidden massage point, Dad.

208
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,240
Hurry up. Press it now!

209
00:16:29,411 --> 00:16:30,840
Use two fingers. Two fingers.

210
00:16:32,958 --> 00:16:34,080
Good. That’s it, son.

211
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:36,041
Almost there.

212
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,001
Is he dead, Dad?

213
00:16:45,334 --> 00:16:46,520
No. He’ll wake up soon.

214
00:16:46,715 --> 00:16:47,760
He’s only unconscious. Go, son.

215
00:16:49,387 --> 00:16:50,640
Hey!

216
00:16:51,718 --> 00:16:53,800
That’s enough! He’s going to die!

217
00:16:58,203 --> 00:16:59,840
You should’ve signed it from the start, you idiot.

218
00:17:00,299 --> 00:17:01,360
Let go of my son right now!

219
00:17:06,331 --> 00:17:08,100
Don’t shoot! He’ll shoot me!

220
00:17:11,835 --> 00:17:13,800
Hattha, take pictures of them.

221
00:17:14,256 --> 00:17:15,257
You need to record everything.

222
00:17:20,253 --> 00:17:21,760
Go! Hurry!

223
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:25,400
Don’t follow us, or I’ll really shoot him!

224
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,400
- Let's go.
- Shit!

225
00:17:43,355 --> 00:17:44,356
Dad, stop here.

226
00:17:45,910 --> 00:17:46,911
Why's that?

227
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:51,000
I have evidence about the building collapse.

228
00:17:51,115 --> 00:17:53,360
Dad, pick up Mom and meet me at the police station.

229
00:17:54,470 --> 00:17:55,471
Wait.

230
00:17:58,123 --> 00:17:59,124
Take this gun with you.

231
00:18:03,024 --> 00:18:04,025
Be careful.

232
00:18:04,944 --> 00:18:05,945
See you there.

233
00:18:19,782 --> 00:18:22,183
You damn masseur. I’m coming for you.

234
00:18:28,806 --> 00:18:31,640
You were more afraid the project would be shut down and you’d lose your job.

235
00:18:32,003 --> 00:18:33,160
- Bastard!
- Oh my son!

236
00:18:37,582 --> 00:18:39,083
- Oh no!
- That guy's Dongyang.

237
00:18:39,416 --> 00:18:41,040
The one whose face we couldn’t see was his guy.

238
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:42,501
He was flat-footed.

239
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:44,680
What does flat-footed mean, Dad?

240
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,050
The arches of his feet were flat, honey.

241
00:19:15,075 --> 00:19:16,076
We have to hurry.

242
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:17,976
Go! Hurry, son!

243
00:19:22,670 --> 00:19:25,240
- Mom! Mom!
- Pha!

244
00:19:25,822 --> 00:19:26,823
Mom!

245
00:19:27,390 --> 00:19:28,391
Pha!

246
00:19:29,363 --> 00:19:31,350
Hey, the gun will be too loud.

247
00:19:33,310 --> 00:19:34,720
Go, honey. Take your mother and run.

248
00:19:53,494 --> 00:19:55,880
Planning to use that video against me, you damn masseur?

249
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,441
Kill them all.

250
00:19:58,971 --> 00:20:00,480
Hattha, take your mother and run!

251
00:20:07,179 --> 00:20:08,180
Mom!

252
00:20:11,723 --> 00:20:13,160
- Get down here.
- Hattha.

253
00:20:13,216 --> 00:20:14,217
No!

254
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:21,311
Mom!

255
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:28,240
[WARNING: The massage techniques depicted in this series are fictional.
Do not attempt to imitate them.]

256
00:20:38,136 --> 00:20:40,080
Hattha, press the point beneath his armpit.

257
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:43,521
[WARNING: The massage techniques depicted in this series are fictional.
Do not attempt to imitate them.]

258
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:50,800
Korn!

259
00:20:51,048 --> 00:20:52,049
Korn!

260
00:20:54,720 --> 00:20:56,000
Hey, let go!

261
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,441
Mom!

262
00:21:08,182 --> 00:21:09,183
Burn this place.

263
00:21:09,446 --> 00:21:11,840
Burn him alive. Let him guard this damn shop.

264
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:16,400
Burn everything down.

265
00:21:32,728 --> 00:21:33,850
Grab him!

266
00:22:12,926 --> 00:22:13,927
You bastards!

267
00:22:16,088 --> 00:22:17,200
That’s a woman and a girl!

268
00:22:17,779 --> 00:22:19,566
Come at me instead! Come on!

269
00:22:20,366 --> 00:22:21,400
Damn it!

270
00:22:28,499 --> 00:22:29,960
Mom! Mom!

271
00:22:35,344 --> 00:22:36,345
Our shop...

272
00:22:39,675 --> 00:22:40,676
Dad!

273
00:22:51,814 --> 00:22:52,815
Hattha!

274
00:22:53,318 --> 00:22:55,040
Run! Run, son!

275
00:22:56,592 --> 00:22:58,320
- Go!
- No, mom! No!

276
00:22:59,171 --> 00:23:01,120
I can't take it anymore. I really can't.

277
00:23:01,619 --> 00:23:04,560
- I don't think I can make it.
- Mom! Come with me.

278
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:06,481
I can’t go on.

279
00:23:07,104 --> 00:23:08,105
I can’t do it.

280
00:23:08,304 --> 00:23:09,440
Go, honey. Go!

281
00:23:10,011 --> 00:23:12,012
Mom, this way!

282
00:23:34,864 --> 00:23:35,865
This way, Mom!

283
00:23:40,630 --> 00:23:42,000
I’ll catch up with you.

284
00:23:53,366 --> 00:23:54,960
Mom, come down!

285
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:02,841
Mom!

286
00:24:05,870 --> 00:24:08,280
Mom! Mom!

287
00:24:13,272 --> 00:24:14,320
Don’t make a sound.

288
00:24:14,952 --> 00:24:16,440
Once they’re gone,

289
00:24:16,611 --> 00:24:18,400
I’ll move this rock off you.

290
00:24:19,112 --> 00:24:20,200
Do my hands smell nice?

291
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:22,300
It’s the scent of the herbs you love.

292
00:24:25,339 --> 00:24:27,200
Hold my hand. Don’t cry.

293
00:24:28,544 --> 00:24:29,545
Mom!

294
00:24:29,808 --> 00:24:30,809
Mom!

295
00:24:34,971 --> 00:24:36,160
Mom!

296
00:24:45,971 --> 00:24:46,972
Flatfoot!

297
00:24:54,883 --> 00:24:56,100
You’re the flat-footed one!

298
00:24:57,491 --> 00:24:58,600
Mom!

299
00:25:00,536 --> 00:25:02,835
Mom! Mom!

300
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:17,955
Back off, you bastard!

301
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,481
Where the hell did he go?

302
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:48,840
Aim at him, you idiot!

303
00:26:04,710 --> 00:26:05,711
Guys!

304
00:26:32,099 --> 00:26:33,100
Asshole!

305
00:26:33,742 --> 00:26:37,040
How dare you mess with me?

306
00:26:42,342 --> 00:26:44,720
Mom! Mom!

307
00:27:13,624 --> 00:27:14,800
What are you doing?

308
00:27:15,624 --> 00:27:16,625
Hey!

309
00:27:17,518 --> 00:27:19,600
Hey, what is going on?

310
00:27:33,435 --> 00:27:34,560
I'm not scared.

311
00:27:35,436 --> 00:27:36,960
You're here with me.

312
00:27:39,843 --> 00:27:41,440
- Does it smell good?
- Yeah.

313
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:50,080
Mommy’s hands smell nice. I’m not scared.

314
00:28:23,550 --> 00:28:25,200
This beach smells fishy, Dad.

315
00:28:26,680 --> 00:28:29,320
You really do have a good nose. I can’t smell anything.

316
00:28:32,030 --> 00:28:34,960
Uncle Korn’s shop is so far away. Who would come all the way out here, Dad?

317
00:28:40,355 --> 00:28:41,356
Hey!

318
00:28:43,336 --> 00:28:44,337
Oh, no!

319
00:29:04,283 --> 00:29:05,284
Korn!

320
00:29:05,387 --> 00:29:06,520
- Korn!
- Hattha!

321
00:29:07,990 --> 00:29:09,600
- Hattha!
- Pha!

322
00:29:15,448 --> 00:29:17,560
Dad, I can smell blood that way.

323
00:29:21,614 --> 00:29:22,615
Son?

324
00:29:23,075 --> 00:29:24,600
Are you sure you can smell blood?

325
00:29:27,902 --> 00:29:28,903
Yes.

326
00:29:39,283 --> 00:29:40,284
It really is blood.

327
00:29:50,408 --> 00:29:52,100
- Dad!
- Be careful, son.

328
00:29:53,912 --> 00:29:55,813
Get behind me and be careful.

329
00:30:02,899 --> 00:30:03,900
Pha.

330
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:07,761
Pha.

331
00:30:08,192 --> 00:30:09,760
Help!

332
00:30:10,363 --> 00:30:11,364
Help!

333
00:30:14,144 --> 00:30:16,760
Help me! Help!

334
00:30:19,518 --> 00:30:20,519
What?

335
00:30:21,828 --> 00:30:22,829
Help!

336
00:30:22,880 --> 00:30:23,881
Hattha?

337
00:30:24,574 --> 00:30:26,480
- Uncle Inn, please help me.
- Hattha.

338
00:30:26,840 --> 00:30:27,841
Hold on, sweetheart.

339
00:30:31,766 --> 00:30:32,800
Watch out.

340
00:30:35,766 --> 00:30:36,767
Come here.

341
00:30:37,750 --> 00:30:38,751
Get up here.

342
00:30:39,987 --> 00:30:40,988
Mom!

343
00:30:41,536 --> 00:30:42,537
Mom!

344
00:30:44,816 --> 00:30:45,817
Mom!

345
00:30:46,582 --> 00:30:47,583
Mom!

346
00:31:02,590 --> 00:31:06,680
The body of the design engineer was found hanging in his room.

347
00:31:06,808 --> 00:31:10,220
He left a letter confessing that his design error caused the building to collapse.

348
00:31:10,558 --> 00:31:11,760
He’s here!

349
00:31:16,759 --> 00:31:20,560
Sir, does this mean the building-collapse case can now be closed?

350
00:31:21,915 --> 00:31:23,739
Under criminal law,

351
00:31:23,776 --> 00:31:27,080
when the offender dies, the criminal case is considered closed.

352
00:31:28,224 --> 00:31:30,480
However, I won’t rush to any conclusions.

353
00:31:30,528 --> 00:31:33,200
We must also be fair to the deceased.

354
00:31:33,542 --> 00:31:37,100
There are still several pieces of evidence that must be examined together,

355
00:31:37,446 --> 00:31:41,480
particularly whether the handwriting in the letter belongs to the deceased.

356
00:31:42,819 --> 00:31:44,680
Please excuse me for a moment.

357
00:31:58,483 --> 00:32:00,880
Is this the way to see Phak, Uncle Inn?

358
00:32:18,900 --> 00:32:20,901
[MORGUE]

359
00:33:03,227 --> 00:33:04,228
Phak.

360
00:34:18,614 --> 00:34:19,615
Let’s go, Hattha.

361
00:34:28,214 --> 00:34:30,040
Notify me immediately once you obtain the arrest warrant.

362
00:34:30,256 --> 00:34:31,520
This is urgent. Do it as quickly as possible.

363
00:34:35,619 --> 00:34:38,400
Wait. I’m afraid neither of you can leave the country yet.

364
00:34:43,840 --> 00:34:46,160
I need both of you to come to the police station

365
00:34:46,331 --> 00:34:47,840
for questioning in connection with a murder case.

366
00:34:48,720 --> 00:34:52,321
Do you have an arrest warrant, Officer?

367
00:34:53,227 --> 00:34:55,800
At this stage, I only want to ask you a few questions.

368
00:34:56,534 --> 00:34:59,100
Then send an official written request to my office.

369
00:34:59,776 --> 00:35:01,360
My lawyer will notify me.

370
00:35:03,099 --> 00:35:04,100
Wait a moment.

371
00:35:04,379 --> 00:35:05,380
Please make way.

372
00:35:06,880 --> 00:35:07,881
I’ve checked.

373
00:35:08,176 --> 00:35:10,069
There is no order prohibiting them from leaving the country.

374
00:35:15,582 --> 00:35:16,800
What does that mean?

375
00:35:17,971 --> 00:35:18,972
We...

376
00:35:19,491 --> 00:35:20,720
We can’t arrest them, sweetheart.

377
00:35:27,115 --> 00:35:28,683
Police Colonel

378
00:35:29,766 --> 00:35:32,167
Krit Teeranasakul,

379
00:35:33,880 --> 00:35:34,881
I hope you’ll be happy.

380
00:35:37,411 --> 00:35:40,160
He killed my mother. He killed my family.

381
00:35:40,424 --> 00:35:42,040
Arrest him! Don’t let him go!

382
00:35:42,062 --> 00:35:45,120
He killed my mother! He killed my brother!

383
00:35:45,523 --> 00:35:48,880
- He killed my mom!
- Hey, you can't accuse me like that.

384
00:35:49,288 --> 00:35:51,320
He killed my whole family.

385
00:35:52,072 --> 00:35:53,440
- Arrest him!
- Go.

386
00:35:53,523 --> 00:35:55,000
Let me go!

387
00:35:55,731 --> 00:35:58,520
He killed my entire family!

388
00:35:59,496 --> 00:36:00,760
Let me go!

389
00:36:03,422 --> 00:36:05,640
Arrest him! Don’t let him get away!

390
00:36:08,016 --> 00:36:10,267
He killed my mother!

391
00:36:33,675 --> 00:36:34,676
Does that feel better?

392
00:36:35,668 --> 00:36:37,400
This is my dad’s shop. You can stop by sometime.

393
00:37:11,982 --> 00:37:12,983
Mom,

394
00:37:13,763 --> 00:37:14,764
Phak,

395
00:37:16,160 --> 00:37:17,480
let's move, okay?

396
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:28,600
[ Ratchaburi ]

397
00:37:48,681 --> 00:37:49,682
Come on, sweetheart.

398
00:38:00,467 --> 00:38:03,480
What if Dad comes home and can’t find us, Uncle Inn?

399
00:38:15,019 --> 00:38:16,080
Minkheng.

400
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:22,040
I have no one left.

401
00:38:23,168 --> 00:38:25,160
Yes, you do. You still have us.

402
00:38:46,795 --> 00:38:47,796
Dad?

403
00:39:15,102 --> 00:39:16,480
Help me, please!

404
00:39:26,595 --> 00:39:27,640
Bring the boat to shore!

405
00:39:28,739 --> 00:39:29,740
Hurry!

406
00:39:37,224 --> 00:39:38,640
Where are the owners of the house?

407
00:39:39,640 --> 00:39:40,641
That girl in red shirt.

408
00:39:52,536 --> 00:39:53,780
Uncle Korn is with me.

409
00:40:00,704 --> 00:40:03,800
Dad, are you hurt? I thought you had left me too.

410
00:40:05,998 --> 00:40:07,160
I’m all right, sweetheart.

411
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:12,001
What about you?

412
00:40:13,001 --> 00:40:14,402
I’m okay.

413
00:40:20,558 --> 00:40:22,080
Your father refused to go to the hospital,

414
00:40:23,459 --> 00:40:25,310
so I treated him traditional way.

415
00:40:53,294 --> 00:40:54,295
I’m sorry.

416
00:41:09,456 --> 00:41:10,680
Dad, are you in pain?

417
00:41:15,302 --> 00:41:16,350
Your father was shot.

418
00:41:19,600 --> 00:41:20,901
The bullet struck his spine.

419
00:41:23,840 --> 00:41:26,641
He’s paralyzed now.

420
00:41:36,551 --> 00:41:40,400
It’s my fault. I couldn’t save your mother or your brother.

421
00:41:41,720 --> 00:41:44,606
No, Dad. It wasn’t your fault. It was theirs.

422
00:41:45,257 --> 00:41:48,040
Don’t cry, Dad. I’m still here with you.

423
00:41:49,651 --> 00:41:52,640
Don’t cry, Dad. I’m here with you.

424
00:41:54,918 --> 00:41:56,560
I’m still here, Dad.

425
00:42:16,904 --> 00:42:18,840
Are you sure it’s in here, Minkheng?

426
00:42:19,704 --> 00:42:22,480
If you mean the old herbal-compress recipes, your dad kept all of them in there.

427
00:42:22,779 --> 00:42:24,100
But what do you need them for?

428
00:42:24,731 --> 00:42:27,100
I’m going to use an herbal-compress recipe to treat Dad.

429
00:42:27,862 --> 00:42:29,867
If your father knew the recipe, surely he would remember it.

430
00:42:30,678 --> 00:42:31,720
Not necessarily.

431
00:42:32,064 --> 00:42:35,240
Dad is distressed about Mom and Phak. He may have forgotten it.

432
00:43:22,065 --> 00:43:23,166
[DO NOT READ]

433
00:43:35,982 --> 00:43:39,620
The point of death is known to all.

434
00:43:40,355 --> 00:43:44,100
But who knows the guiding point that hastens the fall?

435
00:43:44,750 --> 00:43:48,440
Who would press and hold the fatal point?

436
00:43:49,118 --> 00:43:53,120
Press the point beside it, and death shall claim them all.

437
00:44:09,886 --> 00:44:12,140
The Black Book says

438
00:44:12,392 --> 00:44:14,920
massage can be used to kill

439
00:44:15,435 --> 00:44:16,760
if the correct point is pressed.

440
00:44:17,328 --> 00:44:19,200
The fingers must be strong

441
00:44:19,563 --> 00:44:23,120
and powerful enough to apply pressure precisely

442
00:44:23,830 --> 00:44:25,200
to the intended target.

443
00:44:30,515 --> 00:44:33,116
Dad, can massage really kill someone?

444
00:44:35,094 --> 00:44:36,280
Why would you ask that, son?

445
00:44:37,463 --> 00:44:38,464
We heal people.

446
00:44:39,307 --> 00:44:40,440
We don't kill people.

447
00:44:44,544 --> 00:44:46,358
To strengthen your fingers,

448
00:44:46,523 --> 00:44:48,640
you must practice lifting the board every day

449
00:44:49,400 --> 00:44:51,050
while sitting in the full lotus position.

450
00:44:51,800 --> 00:44:52,920
28…

451
00:44:53,376 --> 00:44:55,840
29…30…

452
00:44:57,022 --> 00:44:58,840
Cup your hands,

453
00:44:59,016 --> 00:45:01,120
then lift your body off the ground.

454
00:45:02,019 --> 00:45:03,040
11…

455
00:45:04,496 --> 00:45:05,760
12…

456
00:45:07,960 --> 00:45:09,360
Practice every day

457
00:45:09,998 --> 00:45:11,760
until your thumbs are strong enough

458
00:45:12,526 --> 00:45:14,360
to press the Sen lines with perfect precision.

459
00:46:14,259 --> 00:46:15,260
37…

460
00:46:15,920 --> 00:46:16,921
38…

461
00:46:17,760 --> 00:46:18,761
39…

462
00:46:19,920 --> 00:46:20,921
40…

463
00:46:21,819 --> 00:46:22,820
41…

464
00:46:23,560 --> 00:46:24,561
42…

465
00:46:25,350 --> 00:46:26,351
43…

466
00:46:27,320 --> 00:46:28,321
44…

467
00:46:29,715 --> 00:46:30,716
45…

468
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:36,960
Today marks the auspicious official launch

469
00:46:37,001 --> 00:46:38,904
of the Arokaya Land project.

470
00:46:39,075 --> 00:46:42,320
It is a new, fully integrated wellness center.

471
00:46:42,440 --> 00:46:44,760
Dongyang, a Chinese businessman,

472
00:46:44,872 --> 00:46:47,920
has invested an enormous sum in this project.

473
00:46:48,400 --> 00:46:50,560
Moreover, we are joined by Master Tim,

474
00:46:50,601 --> 00:46:53,202
who is regarded as a grand master of traditional Thai massage

475
00:46:53,250 --> 00:46:56,400
and is highly renowned both in Thailand and abroad.

476
00:46:56,451 --> 00:46:58,640
He has also just completed his latest mission:

477
00:46:58,650 --> 00:47:02,760
a global tour providing therapeutic massage around the world.

478
00:47:02,824 --> 00:47:04,720
Master Tim, may I ask

479
00:47:04,750 --> 00:47:07,320
what made you decide to join Arokaya Land?

480
00:47:07,720 --> 00:47:10,521
I want to preserve Thai wisdom for future generations.

481
00:47:11,100 --> 00:47:12,800
It is my way of giving back to my homeland

482
00:47:13,907 --> 00:47:15,400
so this knowledge can continue to be passed down.

483
00:47:15,726 --> 00:47:18,814
Master Tim, there are rumors that Arokaya Land has a hidden agenda

484
00:47:18,877 --> 00:47:20,400
and may be connected to a casino.

485
00:47:20,472 --> 00:47:23,240
Some say it will tarnish traditional Thai massage by using soft power as a front.

486
00:47:23,320 --> 00:47:24,520
What are your thoughts on these allegations?

487
00:47:25,261 --> 00:47:29,440
Even a tree will flourish if you fertilize it with manure.

488
00:47:30,976 --> 00:47:33,400
Hey, I’m only joking. I was trying to paint a picture.

489
00:47:33,659 --> 00:47:36,336
My sole intention is

490
00:47:36,582 --> 00:47:39,600
to support our massage therapists

491
00:47:39,741 --> 00:47:41,920
and help their profession reach every corner of the world.

492
00:47:42,619 --> 00:47:46,820
And don’t forget, we’re recruiting a new generation of massage therapists

493
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:49,920
to join Arokaya Land.

494
00:47:50,256 --> 00:47:52,350
See? We’re giving the profession our full support.

495
00:47:52,360 --> 00:47:55,000
So, if anyone wants to become a massage therapist under my guidance,

496
00:47:55,574 --> 00:47:56,640
you’re welcome to apply.

497
00:47:59,331 --> 00:48:00,800
- We should apply.
- Let's go.

498
00:48:02,659 --> 00:48:03,660
What a shame.

499
00:48:04,910 --> 00:48:06,240
The whole country respects him,

500
00:48:07,091 --> 00:48:08,192
yet he serves an evil man.

501
00:48:09,300 --> 00:48:11,848
Dongyang has invested far too much in this project.

502
00:48:12,344 --> 00:48:13,571
There’s no way it’s just a wellness center.

503
00:48:14,211 --> 00:48:15,587
They’re definitely hiding a casino inside.

504
00:48:17,600 --> 00:48:19,601
Maybe he’ll only stop committing evil once he’s dead.

505
00:48:20,800 --> 00:48:21,801
Hey!

506
00:48:22,350 --> 00:48:24,651
You’re still thinking about that? You’ll end up in prison.

507
00:48:25,560 --> 00:48:26,915
What about when he killed the people we loved?

508
00:48:27,891 --> 00:48:28,892
He never went to prison.

509
00:48:30,259 --> 00:48:32,360
Then how are we supposed to kill him without going to prison, kiddo?

510
00:48:38,110 --> 00:48:39,600
All right, I have to go.

511
00:48:39,603 --> 00:48:41,400
- Okay?
- Wait.

512
00:48:41,420 --> 00:48:43,600
How many massage therapists are you recruiting, Master Tim?

513
00:48:56,547 --> 00:48:59,480
The ankle is dislocated and twisted out of shape.

514
00:49:02,392 --> 00:49:04,520
- Muk, call the ambulance.
- Got it.

515
00:49:37,272 --> 00:49:38,320
Take him to the hospital.

516
00:49:38,720 --> 00:49:39,721
Okay, sir.

517
00:49:39,795 --> 00:49:41,440
Have a conventional doctor examine him again.

518
00:49:42,435 --> 00:49:44,360
Thank you, Master. Thank you.

519
00:49:45,011 --> 00:49:47,680
That was incredible. He's truly amazing.

520
00:49:47,720 --> 00:49:50,920
See? He’s so skilled that people are willing to pay hundreds of thousands.

521
00:49:51,187 --> 00:49:53,920
Look, it was twisted out of shape just moments ago, and he fixed it right away.

522
00:49:54,120 --> 00:49:55,760
- How could he do that?
- Look!

523
00:50:13,160 --> 00:50:14,161
[FLATFOOT ?]

524
00:50:20,600 --> 00:50:22,087
[DONGYANG JOINS FLOOD-RELIEF EFFORTS]

525
00:50:22,840 --> 00:50:24,000
[SCHOLARSHIP CEREMONY FOR THE FUTURE OF OUR YOUTH]

526
00:50:26,000 --> 00:50:27,001
[INEXPERIENCED NOVICE ENGINEER]

527
00:50:36,200 --> 00:50:37,201
[FLATFOOT ?]

528
00:50:43,846 --> 00:50:46,896
The deadly art of massage is not a method of healing.

529
00:50:47,995 --> 00:50:50,120
It uses knowledge of the body’s tendons,

530
00:50:50,720 --> 00:50:52,440
blood, vital energy,

531
00:50:52,920 --> 00:50:54,440
and pulse points

532
00:50:55,046 --> 00:50:57,000
to transform touch into a weapon

533
00:50:57,447 --> 00:51:01,240
that stops a person’s breath without leaving a wound.

534
00:51:06,800 --> 00:51:09,160
Ittha, Pingkhala,

535
00:51:09,595 --> 00:51:12,080
Sumana, Kalathari,

536
00:51:12,920 --> 00:51:15,160
Sahatsarangsi,

537
00:51:15,730 --> 00:51:18,320
Thawari, Chanthaphusang,

538
00:51:19,000 --> 00:51:21,120
Rucham, Sukhumang, and

539
00:51:21,688 --> 00:51:22,760
Sikhini.

540
00:51:34,710 --> 00:51:37,574
The client requested a young female therapist with a firm touch.

541
00:51:38,357 --> 00:51:41,029
So it’ll have to be you, Hattha.

542
00:51:42,102 --> 00:51:43,103
Leave it to me.

543
00:51:43,355 --> 00:51:44,356
I’m counting on you.

544
00:51:47,800 --> 00:51:48,840
May I?

545
00:52:43,990 --> 00:52:44,991
Hey!

546
00:52:46,678 --> 00:52:47,679
What the hell?

547
00:53:21,198 --> 00:53:22,199
Mom!

548
00:53:32,115 --> 00:53:34,520
Burn him alive. Let him guard this damn shop.

549
00:54:41,027 --> 00:54:42,050
May I?

550
00:54:56,912 --> 00:54:58,320
Sis!

551
00:54:59,104 --> 00:55:01,440
Where did that Chinese client upstairs go?

552
00:55:01,494 --> 00:55:04,480
Where have you been? I had to take over the massage for you.

553
00:55:05,115 --> 00:55:07,880
He had some business to attend to and left before the massage was finished.

554
00:55:08,502 --> 00:55:09,760
- He's gone?
- Yeah.

555
00:55:12,758 --> 00:55:13,759
What's the matter?

556
00:55:54,630 --> 00:55:55,631
Shit!

557
00:56:35,184 --> 00:56:36,185
Hey!

558
00:56:37,552 --> 00:56:39,067
Panic? Are you having a panic attack?

559
00:56:40,560 --> 00:56:42,480
Calm down. Calm down.

560
00:56:44,261 --> 00:56:45,880
It’s okay. Just stay calm.

561
00:56:45,990 --> 00:56:47,840
Look at me. Look at me.

562
00:56:49,200 --> 00:56:50,201
Breathe in.

563
00:56:50,600 --> 00:56:51,601
Breathe out.

564
00:56:51,800 --> 00:56:52,801
Take deep breaths.

565
00:56:53,190 --> 00:56:54,191
In.

566
00:56:54,560 --> 00:56:55,561
Out.

567
00:56:56,246 --> 00:56:57,247
In.

568
00:56:57,798 --> 00:56:58,799
Out.

569
00:57:02,496 --> 00:57:03,497
Just stay calm, okay?

570
00:57:13,710 --> 00:57:14,711
Are you okay?

571
00:57:39,286 --> 00:57:42,440
Arokaya Land is holding auditions for massage therapists tomorrow.

572
00:57:43,614 --> 00:57:45,280
Dongyang and his men are not to be underestimated.

573
00:57:45,300 --> 00:57:47,520
If we want to get close to him, we’ll have to do it through massage, right?

574
00:57:47,840 --> 00:57:49,400
Your muscles are stiff and tense.

575
00:57:49,860 --> 00:57:50,976
It’s as if you’re carrying a heavy burden.

576
00:57:51,061 --> 00:57:52,240
May I take the practical test again?

577
00:57:58,027 --> 00:57:59,028
What are you doing?

578
00:57:59,334 --> 00:58:00,335
Let me help you for a change.
